{
  "name": "ai-prompt-constructor",
  "displayName": "AI Prompt Constructor",
  "description": "Turn rough human intent into a fully structured, role-framed, output-specified prompt for any AI tool.",
  "version": "0.10.0",
  "license": "MIT",
  "publisher": "will-shaffer",
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "^1.95.0",
    "node": ">=20"
  },
  "categories": [
    "Other"
  ],
  "keywords": [
    "prompt",
    "prompt engineering",
    "ai",
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "main": "./dist/extension.js",
  "bin": {
    "promptc": "./dist/cli.js",
    "apc": "./dist/cli.js"
  },
  "exports": {
    "./core": {
      "types": "./src/core/index.ts",
      "require": "./dist/core.js",
      "default": "./dist/core.js"
    }
  },
  "extensionKind": [
    "workspace"
  ],
  "activationEvents": [],
  "contributes": {
    "commands": [
      {
        "command": "promptConstructor.open",
        "title": "Open Prompt Constructor",
        "category": "Prompt Constructor"
      },
      {
        "command": "promptConstructor.compileSelection",
        "title": "Compile Selection Into a Prompt",
        "category": "Prompt Constructor"
      },
      {
        "command": "promptConstructor.setApiKey",
        "title": "Set Anthropic API Key",
        "category": "Prompt Constructor"
      },
      {
        "command": "promptConstructor.clearApiKey",
        "title": "Clear Anthropic API Key",
        "category": "Prompt Constructor"
      },
      {
        "command": "promptConstructor.detectClis",
        "title": "Detect AI CLIs",
        "category": "Prompt Constructor"
      },
      {
        "command": "promptConstructor.chooseBackend",
        "title": "Change Compiling Backend",
        "category": "Prompt Constructor"
      },
      {
        "command": "promptConstructor.chooseModel",
        "title": "Change Compiling Model",
        "category": "Prompt Constructor"
      },
      {
        "command": "promptConstructor.startWorkflow",
        "title": "Start Workflow…",
        "category": "Prompt Constructor"
      }
    ],
    "keybindings": [
      {
        "command": "promptConstructor.open",
        "key": "ctrl+alt+p",
        "mac": "cmd+alt+p"
      }
    ],
    "menus": {
      "editor/context": [
        {
          "command": "promptConstructor.compileSelection",
          "when": "editorHasSelection",
          "group": "1_modification@100"
        }
      ]
    },
    "configuration": {
      "title": "AI Prompt Constructor",
      "properties": {
        "promptConstructor.provider": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "auto",
            "local-cli",
            "copilot",
            "anthropic"
          ],
          "default": "auto",
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Try a local AI CLI first, then the editor's own models, then an Anthropic API key.",
            "Only invoke a local AI CLI you have already signed in to (no API key needed).",
            "Only use language models provided by your editor (no API key needed).",
            "Only use the Anthropic API (requires an API key)."
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "Which backend compiles your prompts. `auto` prefers a local CLI you have already authenticated, because that needs no API key and uses the subscription you already pay for."
        },
        "promptConstructor.anthropic.model": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "claude-sonnet-5",
          "examples": [
            "claude-sonnet-5",
            "claude-haiku-4-5",
            "claude-opus-5"
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "Model used when the Anthropic backend is active.\n\nDefaults to a mid-tier model on purpose: compiling a prompt fills a fixed nine-field schema, which is structured extraction rather than deep reasoning, so the most capable tier is hard to justify as a default when it costs several times more per token. Drop to `claude-haiku-4-5` for the cheapest compiles, or raise to `claude-opus-5` if compiled prompts feel shallow.\n\nThis setting applies **only** to the Anthropic backend. It has no effect when a local CLI or your editor's own models are compiling."
        },
        "promptConstructor.copilot.family": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "",
          "markdownDescription": "Pin a specific model family (for example `claude-sonnet-4.5` or `gpt-4o`). Applies across every provider your editor exposes, not just Copilot. Leave empty to auto-select."
        },
        "promptConstructor.localCli.preset": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "claude-code",
            "codex",
            "opencode",
            "custom"
          ],
          "default": "claude-code",
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Claude Code CLI (`claude -p`).",
            "OpenAI Codex CLI (`codex exec`).",
            "opencode (`opencode run`).",
            "A command you specify in promptConstructor.localCli.command."
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "Which local AI command-line tool to invoke. The tool supplies its own credentials — this extension never reads them."
        },
        "promptConstructor.localCli.path": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "",
          "markdownDescription": "Absolute path to the CLI executable. Leave empty to search `PATH` and common install directories. Set this if detection fails — run **Detect AI CLIs** to see where it looked."
        },
        "promptConstructor.localCli.command": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "",
          "markdownDescription": "Executable name when `promptConstructor.localCli.preset` is `custom`."
        },
        "promptConstructor.localCli.args": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default": [],
          "markdownDescription": "Arguments passed when `promptConstructor.localCli.preset` is `custom`. The prompt is written to the tool's standard input, not appended here."
        },
        "promptConstructor.timeoutSeconds": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 120,
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 900,
          "markdownDescription": "Give up on a compile after this many seconds. Prevents a wedged or blocked request from spinning forever. Set to `0` to disable the timeout entirely."
        },
        "promptConstructor.grounding.enabled": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Read the open workspace (languages, entry points, `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`, directory shape) so generated prompts cite real paths instead of guessing. This is sent only to the model you have already configured."
        },
        "promptConstructor.grounding.maxFiles": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 5000,
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 100000,
          "markdownDescription": "Maximum number of workspace files to scan when building repository context.\n\nThis bounds scan **accuracy**, not prompt size — only aggregates (language counts, directories, entry points) are sent, never the file list, so the context stays roughly the same size regardless. Scanning is cheap: measured at ~25ms for 1,500 files. Set to `0` to disable grounding entirely."
        },
        "promptConstructor.localCli.model": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "",
          "examples": [
            "sonnet",
            "haiku"
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "Model to ask the local CLI for, passed as that tool's model flag. Leave empty to use whatever the tool would pick on its own.\n\nWorth setting: compiling a prompt fills a fixed nine-field schema, and an agentic CLI left to its own default will generally reach for its most capable model. `sonnet` is a good balance; `haiku` is cheapest.\n\nOnly `claude-code` is verified to accept `--model` — the other presets carry the flag from documentation, not measurement."
        }
      }
    }
  },
